# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise of the entangling layers with `qiskit-noise-learning` {#learn-the-noise-of-the-entangling-layers-with-qiskit-noise-learning}"
msgstr "Pelajari hingar lapisan berbelit dengan `qiskit-noise-learning` {#learn-the-noise-of-the-entangling-layers-with-qiskit-noise-learning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEA starts by learning the twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit. We assume a Markovian noise model, and therefore only the noise model of each unique layer of entangling gates should be learned, because the depth of the circuit is assumed to not affect the noise channel of a given entangling layer. The more accurate the learned noise model is, the more accurate the amplification will be.\n"
msgstr "PEA bermula dengan mempelajari model hingar twirled bagi setiap lapisan gate berbelit dalam litar. Kita menganggap model hingar Markovian, dan oleh itu hanya model hingar bagi setiap lapisan gate berbelit yang unik perlu dipelajari, kerana kedalaman litar diandaikan tidak menjejaskan saluran hingar bagi sesuatu lapisan berbelit. Semakin tepat model hingar yang dipelajari, semakin tepat penguatan tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use `qiskit-noise-learning` for learning the noise. The learner repeats each layer `fragment_depths` times in its learning circuits, twirls each circuit `num_randomizations` times, and fits the decay of the measured fidelities to a Pauli-Lindblad model. The following code draws the learned noise model, with the two layers merged into one map. Each qubit is a pie of its weight-1 X, Y, and Z rates summed over the two layers, and each edge shows the learned weight-2 rates; a rate of ``3e-4`` means that error occurs on roughly three of every 10,000 uses of the layer.\n"
msgstr "Kami menggunakan `qiskit-noise-learning` untuk mempelajari hingar. Pembelajar mengulang setiap lapisan sebanyak `fragment_depths` kali dalam litar pembelajarannya, melakukan twirl pada setiap litar sebanyak `num_randomizations` kali, dan memadankan pereputan fidelity yang diukur kepada model Pauli-Lindblad. Kod berikut melukis model hingar yang dipelajari, dengan kedua-dua lapisan digabungkan menjadi satu peta. Setiap qubit ialah carta pai bagi kadar X, Y dan Z berpemberat-1 yang dijumlahkan merentas kedua-dua lapisan, dan setiap sisi menunjukkan kadar berpemberat-2 yang dipelajari; kadar ``3e-4`` bermaksud ralat itu berlaku pada kira-kira tiga daripada setiap 10,000 penggunaan lapisan tersebut.\n"

